1
00:00:03,657 --> 00:00:05,887
What's a four-letter word
for "nonsense"?

2
00:00:06,059 --> 00:00:08,527
- Bull.
- Thanks.

3
00:00:09,329 --> 00:00:11,888
- Mind if we join you?
- No. Sit down.

4
00:00:12,064 --> 00:00:14,328
Selma, you haven't touched your food.

5
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:17,401
I've touched it. I've chewed it.
I've swallowed it.

6
00:00:17,570 --> 00:00:20,562
Now it's up to my enzymes.

7
00:00:20,973 --> 00:00:23,167
That's the judge's tray.
He's on the phone.

8
00:00:23,341 --> 00:00:24,933
Got another lead on those tickets.

9
00:00:25,377 --> 00:00:29,211
I must say, I've never seen anybody
so whipped up about a concert.

10
00:00:29,381 --> 00:00:31,713
Well, you know how he is
about Mel Torme.

11
00:00:31,883 --> 00:00:33,475
Bonkers.

12
00:00:33,652 --> 00:00:35,209
It fits.

13
00:00:35,386 --> 00:00:38,082
Personally, I don't see the big
attraction about Mel Torme.

14
00:00:38,255 --> 00:00:40,086
I like singers that stick to the tune.

15
00:00:40,257 --> 00:00:41,815
Like who, for instance?

16
00:00:41,992 --> 00:00:43,323
Leontyne Price...

17
00:00:43,494 --> 00:00:45,860
...Luciano Pavarotti...

18
00:00:46,029 --> 00:00:48,930
<i>...that bird on Sesame Street's
not bad either.</i>

19
00:00:51,467 --> 00:00:52,832
- Any luck?
- Yeah. All bad.

20
00:00:53,002 --> 00:00:55,027
The concert's been sold out
for two weeks...

21
00:00:55,204 --> 00:00:57,035
...and my sources don't have tickets.

22
00:00:57,206 --> 00:01:00,140
I don't believe it. I am two days
away from getting shut out.

23
00:01:00,308 --> 00:01:02,333
It's only a concert, judge.

24
00:01:02,744 --> 00:01:05,406
No, Liz. Woodstock was only a concert.

25
00:01:05,580 --> 00:01:07,445
This is Mel Torme.

26
00:01:07,816 --> 00:01:09,545
Yeah, I'm into financial planning.

27
00:01:09,718 --> 00:01:13,084
I make money the old-fashioned way.
I print it.

28
00:01:13,254 --> 00:01:16,849
- Dan, you're a very funny guy.
- Yes. Well...

29
00:01:17,024 --> 00:01:19,390
...I have my serious side too.

30
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:21,858
Unhand me, sir. I'll scream.

31
00:01:22,029 --> 00:01:25,930
You'll scream. You'll faint.
You'll see skyrockets going off.

32
00:01:26,766 --> 00:01:28,859
Is it me, or has Dan
been different lately?

33
00:01:29,035 --> 00:01:31,196
No. He's always been different.

34
00:01:32,539 --> 00:01:34,665
You think there's been a little...

35
00:01:34,840 --> 00:01:36,307
...between them?
- Come on, now.

36
00:01:36,475 --> 00:01:39,774
Just because people work together
and have coffee breaks together...

37
00:01:39,945 --> 00:01:41,469
...and laughs, don't jump to...

38
00:01:41,647 --> 00:01:45,139
Don't look now.
He's kissing her hand.

39
00:01:46,351 --> 00:01:49,945
Listen, you lured me in here
with the promise of a cup of coffee.

40
00:01:50,121 --> 00:01:52,316
- Any chance of getting one?
- That's the spirit.

41
00:01:52,490 --> 00:01:54,458
Use me.

42
00:01:57,862 --> 00:02:00,830
- Look at that man smile.
- It's cute.

43
00:02:00,997 --> 00:02:05,832
It's dangerous. Your teeth dry up
and stick to your lips.

44
00:02:06,269 --> 00:02:08,533
Very painful.

45
00:02:10,507 --> 00:02:13,202
- Hey, Dan, over here.
- Dan.

46
00:02:13,375 --> 00:02:16,640
Dan, I think the others
want us to join them.

47
00:02:16,812 --> 00:02:18,871
- Come over.
- Come on over, Dan.

48
00:02:20,015 --> 00:02:22,347
I don't see anyone.

49
00:02:22,518 --> 00:02:25,418
I think you might be right.
It looks like our Dan is in love.

50
00:02:25,587 --> 00:02:27,214
Incredible!

51
00:02:27,388 --> 00:02:29,822
That's it. "Incredible."
How many letters?

52
00:02:30,892 --> 00:02:32,120
Ten.

53
00:02:34,129 --> 00:02:35,857
Close enough.

54
00:03:20,271 --> 00:03:24,468
Has anyone ever told you what
a cute vaccination scar you have?

55
00:03:25,575 --> 00:03:28,043
Not that I recall.

56
00:03:28,611 --> 00:03:30,943
Well, if it isn't two of
the loveliest ladies...

57
00:03:31,114 --> 00:03:33,048
...in the entire criminal justice system.

58
00:03:33,216 --> 00:03:34,478
Hi.

59
00:03:34,884 --> 00:03:37,374
- Dan?
- Dan Fielding?

60
00:03:37,553 --> 00:03:40,750
Liz, that may be the smartest
outfit I've ever seen you wear...

61
00:03:40,923 --> 00:03:43,357
...and you have worn
some smart outfits.

62
00:03:43,525 --> 00:03:48,587
- I have?
- Don't you dare change that hair.

63
00:03:53,167 --> 00:03:57,763
Remember that movie about the pods
in the basement?

64
00:04:00,407 --> 00:04:01,635
Here.

65
00:04:01,808 --> 00:04:03,070
What's this?

66
00:04:03,243 --> 00:04:05,143
A poem I wrote on the subway
this morning.

67
00:04:05,312 --> 00:04:06,540
Oh?

68
00:04:10,383 --> 00:04:11,679
What do you think?

69
00:04:12,518 --> 00:04:14,213
Nice.

70
00:04:14,386 --> 00:04:18,447
Must be hard to find something
to rhyme with "jurisprudence."

71
00:04:20,025 --> 00:04:22,516
Looks like love is in
full bloom over there.

72
00:04:22,695 --> 00:04:25,595
The massive amounts of fertilizer
have helped, I think.

73
00:04:25,763 --> 00:04:27,924
- Come on, Miss Wagner.
- Don't be so hard on him.

74
00:04:28,099 --> 00:04:30,499
Haven't you ever been
madly in love with someone?

75
00:04:30,668 --> 00:04:33,432
Of course not. I'm engaged.

76
00:04:33,605 --> 00:04:36,232
What I mean is, I don't think
that it's appropriate...

77
00:04:36,406 --> 00:04:38,567
...for people who work together
to have...

78
00:04:38,742 --> 00:04:41,267
...romantic relationships.

79
00:04:41,979 --> 00:04:43,844
- Have you?
- Have I what?

80
00:04:44,014 --> 00:04:46,244
Have you ever been
madly in love with someone?

81
00:04:46,416 --> 00:04:48,349
- Sure.
- Anyone I know?

82
00:04:48,517 --> 00:04:50,610
I doubt it. She was
a cute dark-haired girl...

83
00:04:50,786 --> 00:04:52,617
...who sat next to me
in second grade.

84
00:04:52,788 --> 00:04:55,382
- I see.
- I forget her name, but she was wild.

85
00:04:55,558 --> 00:04:57,025
- Your Honor...
- We'd sneak off...

86
00:04:57,193 --> 00:05:00,423
...to the cloakroom and eat paste.
- Next case.

87
00:05:00,829 --> 00:05:03,024
You see, in our version of hide-and-seek...

88
00:05:03,198 --> 00:05:05,029
<i>The People v. Leo Bell, Your Honor.</i>

89
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:07,828
Mr. Bell was arrested near
Madison Square Garden...

90
00:05:08,003 --> 00:05:09,300
...for scalping tickets.

91
00:05:09,471 --> 00:05:12,633
Hey, I'm very distraught
about this whole thing, judge.

92
00:05:12,806 --> 00:05:14,671
See, I made my little niece a promise:

93
00:05:14,842 --> 00:05:18,938
The next time the ice show comes to town,
her Uncle Leo would take her.

94
00:05:19,113 --> 00:05:22,879
But then two weeks ago,
something else took her.

95
00:05:23,050 --> 00:05:25,449
- I'm sorry. You mean...?
- She went with the school...

96
00:05:25,618 --> 00:05:28,109
...and I got stuck
with the ticket, right.

97
00:05:28,688 --> 00:05:30,485
You thought you might sell the ticket?

98
00:05:30,657 --> 00:05:32,090
Exactly.

99
00:05:32,258 --> 00:05:35,159
So someone else's niece
could enjoy the show.

100
00:05:35,328 --> 00:05:37,989
That is a very nice thought, Mr. Bell,
but it says here...

101
00:05:38,163 --> 00:05:41,030
...that you sold a $9 ticket for $45.

102
00:05:41,199 --> 00:05:44,362
Well, that seat was right behind
Snoopy's doghouse.

103
00:05:45,904 --> 00:05:49,339
If it please the court, Exhibit A
was taken from the defendant...

104
00:05:49,507 --> 00:05:51,771
...at the time of his arrest.

105
00:05:52,643 --> 00:05:55,908
I couldn't have said it better myself.

106
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:58,344
Well, how do you explain this, Mr. Bell?

107
00:05:58,516 --> 00:06:00,380
You must have 200 or 300 tickets here.

108
00:06:01,184 --> 00:06:03,084
I love the theater.

109
00:06:03,954 --> 00:06:07,651
Your appreciation of the arts
is duly noted for the record.

110
00:06:07,824 --> 00:06:13,056
- Your hair smells great.
- It's dandruff shampoo.

111
00:06:14,496 --> 00:06:17,556
Excuse me, does the prosecution
have anything else to present?

112
00:06:17,733 --> 00:06:19,758
- Your Honor...
- Your Honor... Sorry, go ahead.

113
00:06:19,935 --> 00:06:21,800
No, no. After you.

114
00:06:22,538 --> 00:06:25,233
Mr. Bell is so brazen
in his flaunting of the law...

115
00:06:25,406 --> 00:06:28,534
...that he prints business cards
listing his office phone number...

116
00:06:28,710 --> 00:06:31,975
...which is, in fact, a phone booth
on Lexington Avenue.

117
00:06:34,048 --> 00:06:36,948
This is quite an assortment
you have here, Mr. Bell:

118
00:06:37,117 --> 00:06:41,611
<i>The Knicks, the Rangers, the boat show,
La Cage aux Folles, Mel...</i>

119
00:06:42,856 --> 00:06:45,723
...Torme?

120
00:06:45,892 --> 00:06:48,860
There must be 30 Mel Torme tickets here.

121
00:06:49,028 --> 00:06:54,091
I had 50 Tormes this morning.
That is a very hot ticket.

122
00:06:55,368 --> 00:06:58,769
- Your Honor.
- September 13.

123
00:06:58,938 --> 00:07:00,962
- Beg your pardon?
- That's when Mel Torme...

124
00:07:01,139 --> 00:07:03,039
...was born in Chicago.

125
00:07:03,208 --> 00:07:05,176
- I celebrate it every year.
- Your Honor...

126
00:07:05,343 --> 00:07:08,403
I mean, I don't have a big affair.
It's not a national holiday...

127
00:07:08,580 --> 00:07:10,013
...not yet.

128
00:07:10,548 --> 00:07:12,243
Sir, the case.

129
00:07:12,417 --> 00:07:15,647
- Is open-and-shut, right, Leo?
- I have erred.

130
00:07:15,819 --> 00:07:17,309
Forgive me.

131
00:07:17,488 --> 00:07:19,922
Fifty dollars penance.

132
00:07:20,090 --> 00:07:21,557
Go in peace.

133
00:07:22,259 --> 00:07:24,318
I like him. He's nuts.

134
00:07:25,194 --> 00:07:27,185
Let's have a recess.

135
00:07:27,363 --> 00:07:28,796
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

136
00:07:28,965 --> 00:07:31,058
Your thinking was clear,
your logic, precise.

137
00:07:31,234 --> 00:07:33,862
You're a credit to the profession.
Let's have children.

138
00:07:34,537 --> 00:07:38,939
- Oh, Dan.
- Oh, Suzanne.

139
00:07:42,244 --> 00:07:44,872
- Harry, they're evidence.
- Of course.

140
00:07:45,047 --> 00:07:47,481
I have to turn them over
to the city property clerk.

141
00:07:47,649 --> 00:07:50,082
- Absolutely. That's the law.
- Right.

142
00:07:51,085 --> 00:07:54,077
Oh, God. Row B.

143
00:07:59,293 --> 00:08:01,590
- Your Honor?
- Miss Woodfield?

144
00:08:01,761 --> 00:08:04,423
I'm sorry, but I couldn't
help overhearing, and...

145
00:08:04,898 --> 00:08:07,423
...well, I have two tickets
to the Mel Torme concert.

146
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:10,933
- You're not using them? Fantastic!
- No. I'm using them...

147
00:08:11,104 --> 00:08:13,401
At least one of them.
See, I'm a big fan too.

148
00:08:13,572 --> 00:08:15,540
- Really?
- I wondered if you might wanna...

149
00:08:15,707 --> 00:08:18,005
...use the other ticket.
- But what about Dan?

150
00:08:18,444 --> 00:08:22,039
- What about him?
- I assumed you two were...

151
00:08:22,214 --> 00:08:25,410
Oh, no, no. I mean, he's a very nice guy.

152
00:08:25,583 --> 00:08:28,108
We've gone out a couple of times,
but it's not serious.

153
00:08:28,286 --> 00:08:30,880
- Well, in that case...
- You'll go with me?

154
00:08:31,055 --> 00:08:34,388
I would go with Godzilla.

155
00:08:37,160 --> 00:08:40,061
I have better breath.

156
00:08:40,230 --> 00:08:43,199
- I meant...
- I know what you meant.

157
00:08:43,366 --> 00:08:45,027
Your Honor...

158
00:08:45,202 --> 00:08:47,329
...is she adorable or what?

159
00:08:47,504 --> 00:08:49,199
The court agrees, Mr. Fielding.

160
00:08:49,371 --> 00:08:52,807
I'll tell you what. After work
why don't we go get pizza. My treat.

161
00:08:52,975 --> 00:08:54,272
I'd love to, but I can't.

162
00:08:54,443 --> 00:08:56,377
I'm already doing something this evening.

163
00:08:56,545 --> 00:08:58,843
Yeah. We're already doing
something this evening.

164
00:08:59,014 --> 00:09:01,811
What exactly will we be doing this evening?

165
00:09:01,983 --> 00:09:03,883
Sorry, Dan. I have a date.

166
00:09:04,052 --> 00:09:07,180
A couple of the gals are getting together,
doing their nails.

167
00:09:07,355 --> 00:09:10,119
- That kind of thing?
- No. It's a date.

168
00:09:12,594 --> 00:09:14,754
With a man?

169
00:09:14,928 --> 00:09:16,327
Are you serious?

170
00:09:16,497 --> 00:09:18,362
Deadly. Who are you going out with?

171
00:09:18,532 --> 00:09:20,557
- None of your business.
- Come on. Tell me.

172
00:09:20,734 --> 00:09:23,066
- I won't die.
- Excuse me.

173
00:09:23,237 --> 00:09:26,535
Shall I pick you up at your house,
or should we just leave from here?

174
00:09:28,908 --> 00:09:30,398
Him?!

175
00:09:31,144 --> 00:09:33,203
Could we discuss this
somewhere else, Bull?

176
00:09:33,379 --> 00:09:35,540
Excuse us.

177
00:09:40,452 --> 00:09:41,749
Dan?

178
00:09:43,054 --> 00:09:44,578
Dan, I didn't know.

179
00:09:44,756 --> 00:09:46,917
I didn't know that you
and Suzanne were serious.

180
00:09:47,092 --> 00:09:50,322
- I just thought that...
- Harry, stuff it.

181
00:09:53,397 --> 00:09:55,831
- I can't believe he said that.
- No, it's okay.

182
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,093
I told him he could call me "Harry."

183
00:10:04,407 --> 00:10:07,069
I have never known Dan to be late before.

184
00:10:07,243 --> 00:10:10,508
- I hope he's all right.
- Yeah. But it's his own fault.

185
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:15,309
I mean, I always make it a rule: Never get
involved with people I work with.

186
00:10:16,118 --> 00:10:19,815
You work with rapists, junkies,
muggers and flashers.

187
00:10:22,124 --> 00:10:24,285
That does make it easier.

188
00:10:27,361 --> 00:10:30,262
- Hi, Dan. How was dinner?
- The part that stayed down? Fine.

189
00:10:30,431 --> 00:10:31,796
Dan.

190
00:10:32,967 --> 00:10:35,162
Dan, I've gotta talk to you
about something.

191
00:10:35,336 --> 00:10:36,928
- Business?
- No.

192
00:10:37,104 --> 00:10:39,264
Catch me in the fall.

193
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:43,303
- Dan, can we talk?
- Sure.

194
00:10:45,979 --> 00:10:49,540
So where are you and Conehead
the Barbarian going tonight?

195
00:10:52,084 --> 00:10:54,211
Dan, it is just a dinner date.

196
00:10:54,386 --> 00:10:56,786
Foraging in the forest,
trapping small animals...

197
00:10:56,956 --> 00:10:58,253
...that kind of thing?

198
00:10:58,924 --> 00:11:01,324
If you must know, he's taking me
to the restaurant...

199
00:11:01,493 --> 00:11:03,619
...on top of
the World Trade Center.

200
00:11:04,495 --> 00:11:06,258
Are you going to use the elevator...

201
00:11:06,431 --> 00:11:09,195
...or is he just dragging you
up the side of the building?

202
00:11:11,302 --> 00:11:13,463
- Poor guy.
- Yeah.

203
00:11:13,638 --> 00:11:15,298
I'm sure he presumed way too much...

204
00:11:15,472 --> 00:11:17,997
...but he must feel like he's been
kicked in the teeth.

205
00:11:18,175 --> 00:11:20,871
- Well...
- I'm sure that to feel that a friend...

206
00:11:21,044 --> 00:11:23,205
...has stabbed you in the heart...
- But...

207
00:11:23,380 --> 00:11:27,315
- Betrayal eats away so...
- I didn't know!

208
00:11:28,451 --> 00:11:31,443
That we were getting so backed up!

209
00:11:31,621 --> 00:11:33,452
Next case!

210
00:11:33,623 --> 00:11:36,490
That would be Gerald Jackson,
Your Honor...

211
00:11:36,659 --> 00:11:38,751
...charged with theft, second-degree.

212
00:11:38,927 --> 00:11:42,886
He was accused of tapping the till of
his employer, the Midtown Speedy Mart.

213
00:11:43,064 --> 00:11:44,964
- Miss Williams?
- Yes, sir. Your Honor...

214
00:11:45,133 --> 00:11:47,465
...the amount of money
is less than $50...

215
00:11:47,636 --> 00:11:50,366
...and my client has expressed
willingness to pay it back.

216
00:11:50,537 --> 00:11:52,095
Pay it back?

217
00:11:52,806 --> 00:11:56,537
How do you pay back someone's trust
once you've spent it?

218
00:11:56,710 --> 00:11:59,804
- Mr. Fielding...
- Look at it from my point of view.

219
00:11:59,980 --> 00:12:03,142
I was nuts about her. No.
Scratch that. Insane about her.

220
00:12:03,316 --> 00:12:06,547
I gave her all of my love, all of my
attention, all of my affection...

221
00:12:06,719 --> 00:12:08,311
...and what happens?
She dumps me...

222
00:12:08,488 --> 00:12:11,150
...for Bobbo the Human Redwood
over there.

223
00:12:15,193 --> 00:12:17,093
- I don't feel well.
- I know, Dan...

224
00:12:17,262 --> 00:12:19,127
...but we have to put
personal problems...

225
00:12:19,298 --> 00:12:22,756
- I am going to soil your bench.
- Recess now.

226
00:12:26,538 --> 00:12:29,028
Dan, we've all been through rejection.

227
00:12:29,206 --> 00:12:31,674
Hasn't anything like this
ever happened to you before?

228
00:12:31,842 --> 00:12:33,070
Are you serious?

229
00:12:33,244 --> 00:12:38,011
Harry, I was just jilted in favor of a man
who wears hunting socks to work every day.

230
00:12:38,882 --> 00:12:41,407
Now, be fair.
Bull has his share of talents.

231
00:12:41,584 --> 00:12:45,543
I don't consider being able to drive in
nails with your fists a talent.

232
00:12:46,356 --> 00:12:49,792
Dan, Suzanne appears to be
a wonderful woman.

233
00:12:49,959 --> 00:12:53,325
You know, I really, really thought
that we were simpatico, Harry.

234
00:12:53,495 --> 00:12:54,985
She appeals to a lot of people.

235
00:12:55,164 --> 00:12:57,189
We shared so many of the same interests.

236
00:12:57,366 --> 00:12:59,266
I imagine a lot of people appeal to her.

237
00:12:59,435 --> 00:13:00,959
She found my jokes amusing.

238
00:13:01,136 --> 00:13:03,365
She likes Torme. I like Torme.

239
00:13:03,538 --> 00:13:05,836
Her nose wrinkles when she laughs at them.

240
00:13:06,007 --> 00:13:08,567
- Harry, Suzanne and l...
- Suzanne and l...

241
00:13:08,743 --> 00:13:10,267
Go ahead.

242
00:13:10,445 --> 00:13:13,346
Dan, I'm gonna go...

243
00:13:13,715 --> 00:13:15,443
Answer the door.

244
00:13:17,517 --> 00:13:19,747
- Bull.
- Your Honor.

245
00:13:20,754 --> 00:13:22,619
<i>You're ocupado.</i>

246
00:13:27,193 --> 00:13:28,683
- I'll come back.
- No, no.

247
00:13:28,861 --> 00:13:30,692
Come on in. Come on in.

248
00:13:30,863 --> 00:13:33,093
I think we have something
to talk about.

249
00:13:34,500 --> 00:13:35,728
What?

250
00:13:36,335 --> 00:13:39,303
The year in combs.
You ever see one up close?

251
00:13:41,339 --> 00:13:44,240
Listen, you myopic little dilettante!

252
00:13:45,243 --> 00:13:47,302
Who are you calling little?!

253
00:13:47,479 --> 00:13:48,810
Okay, that is enough of that.

254
00:13:48,980 --> 00:13:51,607
I won't tolerate personal
disagreements that interfere...

255
00:13:51,782 --> 00:13:55,240
...with the operation of my court.
Do I make myself clear?

256
00:13:55,719 --> 00:13:59,086
Now, the three of us have a problem.
We must work it out like grown men.

257
00:13:59,256 --> 00:14:02,555
- The three of us?
- Yeah. We all...

258
00:14:03,926 --> 00:14:07,453
Anybody want pretzels?
Or nuts? I got some avocado dip.

259
00:14:07,630 --> 00:14:09,427
Your Honor, I have cases to prepare.

260
00:14:09,599 --> 00:14:13,091
Why don't you just sit down
until you're told to leave?

261
00:14:14,937 --> 00:14:17,029
You talking to me?

262
00:14:18,840 --> 00:14:21,502
- Guys.
- Perhaps you'd like to step outside.

263
00:14:21,843 --> 00:14:23,708
- You bet I would.
- All right, that's it.

264
00:14:23,879 --> 00:14:26,973
- Nobody leaves here.
- Thank you. Thank you.

265
00:14:31,485 --> 00:14:34,818
Now, we got to find a way
to cut this tension.

266
00:14:37,191 --> 00:14:39,886
Let's hold hands.

267
00:14:42,595 --> 00:14:44,062
What did he say?

268
00:14:44,230 --> 00:14:46,357
I took a sensitivity training
class once...

269
00:14:46,533 --> 00:14:49,093
...and I learned that most male
aggression is due to...

270
00:14:49,269 --> 00:14:51,396
...a lack of physical
and emotional contact...

271
00:14:51,571 --> 00:14:53,299
...with members of the same sex.

272
00:14:53,472 --> 00:14:56,964
Perhaps you should visit
our holding cell sometime, sir.

273
00:14:57,142 --> 00:14:59,804
Come on. You've seen
professional football huddles...

274
00:14:59,978 --> 00:15:03,209
...haven't you? Come on. Come on.

275
00:15:04,816 --> 00:15:07,080
That's it.

276
00:15:08,019 --> 00:15:10,010
Dan, take my hand.

277
00:15:11,589 --> 00:15:14,149
Good. Now, Bull.

278
00:15:15,560 --> 00:15:17,584
All right, now the two of you link up.

279
00:15:18,195 --> 00:15:19,685
Go ahead.

280
00:15:22,065 --> 00:15:24,226
That's it.

281
00:15:24,401 --> 00:15:26,232
No.

282
00:15:26,403 --> 00:15:28,063
I wanna be on top.

283
00:15:32,908 --> 00:15:35,638
Okay, guys.
Now, no need to say anything.

284
00:15:35,811 --> 00:15:38,405
Just let go.

285
00:15:38,581 --> 00:15:41,743
Just feel, experience the bond.

286
00:15:41,916 --> 00:15:44,942
His bond is breaking my knuckles.

287
00:15:45,820 --> 00:15:48,516
Bull, loosen up.

288
00:15:48,690 --> 00:15:51,659
Come on now, guys, relax.
Close your eyes.

289
00:15:52,426 --> 00:15:54,087
All the way.

290
00:15:55,362 --> 00:15:59,162
All right. Now just...

291
00:15:59,333 --> 00:16:01,062
...feel.

292
00:16:04,737 --> 00:16:07,638
Someone came in.

293
00:16:07,807 --> 00:16:09,331
- Hello?
- We'll come back.

294
00:16:09,509 --> 00:16:11,704
- No, no. Don't be silly.
- We were...

295
00:16:11,878 --> 00:16:14,472
...just discussing humiliation.

296
00:16:14,647 --> 00:16:15,875
If you'll all excuse me.

297
00:16:16,048 --> 00:16:18,345
Dan, there is no reason
to feel humiliated.

298
00:16:18,517 --> 00:16:22,180
Some helpful advice:
Date within your species.

299
00:16:23,922 --> 00:16:26,914
I have no idea what she sees in him.

300
00:16:27,959 --> 00:16:31,223
Don't worry.
Women are still tops in my book.

301
00:16:32,863 --> 00:16:35,991
We were just trying
a little sensitivity exercise.

302
00:16:36,166 --> 00:16:38,225
- Just say, "Of course."
- Of course.

303
00:16:38,402 --> 00:16:39,630
Did you want to see me?

304
00:16:39,803 --> 00:16:42,032
Yes. Harry, we're ready
for you anytime you are.

305
00:16:42,205 --> 00:16:43,729
- Fine.
- And I want to apologize...

306
00:16:43,907 --> 00:16:45,374
...for what happened in court.

307
00:16:45,542 --> 00:16:48,409
- I feel partly responsible.
- No, it wasn't your fault.

308
00:16:48,578 --> 00:16:52,513
It's just that Dan needs to realize
that I care as much for him as I do for Bull.

309
00:16:52,681 --> 00:16:54,979
It just so happens
I have a lot of interests.

310
00:16:55,150 --> 00:16:57,675
- Fine.
- Bull likes Post-lmpressionist painters.

311
00:16:57,853 --> 00:16:59,445
- So do I.
- He does?

312
00:16:59,621 --> 00:17:02,556
- Dan enjoys oompah bands. So do I.
- He does.

313
00:17:02,724 --> 00:17:05,385
You and I love Mel Torme,
so we're going to the concert...

314
00:17:05,560 --> 00:17:08,529
...just to have a good time.
- You are?

315
00:17:09,664 --> 00:17:13,828
- Lana, you wanna hear a funny story?
- Yeah. Make me laugh.

316
00:17:14,902 --> 00:17:16,732
Your Honor, you better hurry. It's bad.

317
00:17:16,903 --> 00:17:19,428
- What happened? Bad?
- Bull and Dan in the cafeteria...

318
00:17:19,606 --> 00:17:21,233
...they are fighting.
- Fighting?!

319
00:17:21,408 --> 00:17:24,502
I passed by. Bull was throwing
Dan around like a little rag doll.

320
00:17:24,678 --> 00:17:26,305
- Oh, my God!
- Those stupid...!

321
00:17:26,479 --> 00:17:29,311
- Are they fighting over me?
- Chivalry is not dead.

322
00:17:29,481 --> 00:17:30,743
Let's go.

323
00:17:33,619 --> 00:17:35,109
No. Dan!

324
00:17:35,287 --> 00:17:38,051
He was lucky there was a doctor here.

325
00:17:39,325 --> 00:17:40,815
Look at this place!

326
00:17:40,992 --> 00:17:42,687
Love stinks.

327
00:17:43,394 --> 00:17:46,921
- Is he all right, doctor?
- Couple of cracked ribs, that's all.

328
00:17:47,098 --> 00:17:49,828
You big, overgrown oaf!
How could you?!

329
00:17:50,001 --> 00:17:53,163
Settle down there, Your Honor.
He probably saved this man's life.

330
00:17:53,337 --> 00:17:55,669
- Come again?
- Your friend here almost choked...

331
00:17:55,839 --> 00:17:58,239
...to death on an olive
that got stuck in his throat.

332
00:17:58,408 --> 00:18:01,434
- You mean Bull?
- Applied the Heimlich maneuver...

333
00:18:01,612 --> 00:18:04,410
...with ferocity heretofore
unknown to mankind.

334
00:18:06,482 --> 00:18:08,712
Dan, how do you feel?

335
00:18:09,285 --> 00:18:11,378
Take a guess.

336
00:18:12,388 --> 00:18:14,288
Bull saved your life.

337
00:18:14,457 --> 00:18:15,890
I know.

338
00:18:16,058 --> 00:18:17,285
Bull?

339
00:18:20,895 --> 00:18:24,194
- Yeah?
- Thank you.

340
00:18:24,366 --> 00:18:27,233
Bull, I am so sorry
for what I thought and what I said.

341
00:18:27,836 --> 00:18:30,827
That enough manly affection
for you, Your Honor?

342
00:18:31,972 --> 00:18:33,269
I deserved that.

343
00:18:33,440 --> 00:18:37,376
- Any bandages or tape around here?
- In the guard's lounge. Follow me.

344
00:18:37,544 --> 00:18:39,273
Now, just keep still.

345
00:18:39,446 --> 00:18:41,709
And please, no more help.

346
00:18:43,516 --> 00:18:46,747
Bull, I said some pretty nasty things.

347
00:18:46,919 --> 00:18:51,185
- You didn't say anything that nasty.
- Not to your face, no.

348
00:18:52,191 --> 00:18:53,555
Well, forget it.

349
00:18:53,725 --> 00:18:57,525
No, no! I don't wanna forget it.
I want a chance to make it up to you.

350
00:18:57,696 --> 00:18:58,924
So...

351
00:19:00,332 --> 00:19:03,233
...you can have Suzanne.

352
00:19:04,236 --> 00:19:05,702
He what?

353
00:19:05,870 --> 00:19:08,270
No, Dan, I mean, you were
there first. I had no idea.

354
00:19:08,439 --> 00:19:09,997
- You should have her.
- No, no, no.

355
00:19:10,174 --> 00:19:12,472
- I insist.
- You insist?!

356
00:19:12,643 --> 00:19:15,111
- Listen...
- My ribs, my ribs!

357
00:19:17,714 --> 00:19:20,114
For your information, boys...

358
00:19:20,283 --> 00:19:22,649
...l'm not a plaything
to be tossed around...

359
00:19:22,819 --> 00:19:25,344
...between the two of you.
I'm an adult...

360
00:19:25,522 --> 00:19:28,150
...and I'll make the decisions
about what I do in life...

361
00:19:28,324 --> 00:19:31,417
...thank you, including whom
I spend my time with.

362
00:19:31,593 --> 00:19:34,756
Now, can't you just accept the fact
that I liked all three of you...

363
00:19:34,930 --> 00:19:36,830
...that's why I wanted to be with you?

364
00:19:41,969 --> 00:19:44,563
Three?

365
00:19:47,709 --> 00:19:49,700
Isn't that amazing? She...

366
00:19:49,877 --> 00:19:52,368
She just happened to have
an extra seat to the...

367
00:19:52,547 --> 00:19:54,377
...Mel Torme concert.

368
00:19:55,682 --> 00:19:58,776
Is that something?
Or is that something?

369
00:19:59,286 --> 00:20:01,652
Come on, Harry. You're not
gonna back out, are you?

370
00:20:01,822 --> 00:20:06,554
No. It's just that when we've had some
time to put all this in perspective...

371
00:20:06,726 --> 00:20:09,991
Listen, I'm going.
You can do whatever you want.

372
00:20:12,298 --> 00:20:14,323
Bull?

373
00:20:15,501 --> 00:20:17,833
Dan?

374
00:20:20,705 --> 00:20:24,334
- I'm sorry, Suzanne.
- No, no. You own that ticket now.

375
00:20:29,214 --> 00:20:31,078
There. You satisfied?

376
00:20:31,248 --> 00:20:34,376
You could tape that sucker
back together real easy.

377
00:20:34,818 --> 00:20:37,810
I would have hoped that a gesture
of friendship was enough...

378
00:20:37,988 --> 00:20:40,354
...but evidently you guys want blood.

379
00:20:46,963 --> 00:20:48,225
There.

380
00:20:48,397 --> 00:20:50,558
Now are you happy?

381
00:20:50,733 --> 00:20:52,860
That was dumb.

382
00:20:53,035 --> 00:20:54,433
She's right, Harry.

383
00:20:54,603 --> 00:20:56,332
- She is?
- Suzanne, you were correct.

384
00:20:56,505 --> 00:21:01,135
I acted like a stereotypical
male chauvinist pig...

385
00:21:01,309 --> 00:21:04,142
...and I apologize.
- Yeah. Me too, Suzanne.

386
00:21:04,312 --> 00:21:07,109
I guess it got a little crazy around here.

387
00:21:07,281 --> 00:21:08,748
It won't happen again.

388
00:21:08,916 --> 00:21:12,545
Well, gentlemen, I appreciate
your apologies. I accept.

389
00:21:12,720 --> 00:21:15,188
So, what you are all saying is...

390
00:21:15,356 --> 00:21:17,756
- Go with her. Have fun.
- Go ahead.

391
00:21:24,330 --> 00:21:26,696
If you'll excuse me.

392
00:21:27,200 --> 00:21:31,260
Harry, I think Mel put it best
once when he said:

393
00:21:44,048 --> 00:21:46,539
- Hi, everything's locked up.
- Good.

394
00:21:46,717 --> 00:21:48,548
We're all going to Emilio's for a beer.

395
00:21:48,719 --> 00:21:50,812
- Wanna join us?
- Not tonight, Lana. Thanks.

396
00:21:51,989 --> 00:21:55,788
- It's been a crazy couple of days.
- Yeah.

397
00:21:57,460 --> 00:22:01,157
- Dan's coming back tomorrow.
- Great, great, great.

398
00:22:01,331 --> 00:22:04,061
Harry, I want you to know
I'm sorry about the concert.

399
00:22:04,234 --> 00:22:06,701
I know. I'm fine.
Really, thanks.

400
00:22:08,838 --> 00:22:11,136
Unless there's something else...

401
00:22:11,307 --> 00:22:14,708
No, no. Nothing.

402
00:22:16,645 --> 00:22:19,306
- See you tomorrow.
- See you tomorrow.

403
00:22:19,480 --> 00:22:20,947
Fine.

404
00:22:41,034 --> 00:22:44,730
<i>Ladies and gentlemen, Mr. Mel Torme!</i>

405
00:22:44,904 --> 00:22:46,895
<i>One, two...</i>

406
00:22:47,874 --> 00:22:49,808
<i>Thank you, ladies and gentlemen.</i>

407
00:22:50,343 --> 00:22:53,437
<i>Now, there's good vibes tonight.</i>

